From: Chien Wong <m@xv97.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wifi: mac80211: reserve enough tailroom for a 256-bit MME

BIP-CMAC-256 and BIP-GMAC-256 build a 26-byte MME, but
IEEE80211_ENCRYPT_TAILROOM is 18, sized for the 802.11w maximum of the
original BIP ciphers.  The shortfall is currently hidden by the kmalloc
size-class rounding on dev_alloc_skb() and by the 256-byte TIM allowance
in the beacon path, neither of which is a guarantee.

Raise the reservation to 26 so that every path which adds IEEE80211_MMIE
has room for it.

Upstream: c49f54fd2abf ("wifi: mac80211: fix encryption tailroom")

--- a/net/mac80211/ieee80211_i.h
+++ b/net/mac80211/ieee80211_i.h
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ struct ieee80211_mesh_fast_tx;
 
 /* Required encryption head and tailroom */
 #define IEEE80211_ENCRYPT_HEADROOM 8
-#define IEEE80211_ENCRYPT_TAILROOM 18
+#define IEEE80211_ENCRYPT_TAILROOM 26 /* current max: GMAC/CMAC-256 MME */
 
 /* power level hasn't been configured (or set to automatic) */
 #define IEEE80211_UNSET_POWER_LEVEL	INT_MIN
